   =========================================================
   CSS NOTES: Sibling (General Sibling) Combinator (~)

   Definition:
   The sibling combinator (~) selects all elements that come
   after another element and share the same parent.

   Syntax:
   A ~ B

   Meaning:
   Selects every B element that appears after A.

   Rules:
   - Both elements must have the same parent
   - B must come after A in the HTML
   - Selects ALL following siblings
   - Does not select previous elements

   Example:
   h2 ~ p {
     color: green;
   }

   HTML:
   <h2>Heading</h2>
   <p>Paragraph 1</p>
   <p>Paragraph 2</p>
   <p>Paragraph 3</p>

   Class Example:
   .box ~ .box {
     border: 1px solid black;
   }

   Difference from Adjacent Sibling:
   +  Adjacent sibling → only next element
   ~  Sibling combinator → all following elements

   Summary:
   A ~ B selects all B elements that come after A.
   ========================================================= 
